From ed37ea83175329745fe3162f246e6eeafe512a9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alberto Cavalcante <54247214+albertocavalcante@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Feb 2026 11:08:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add OnFunctionEnter/Exit callbacks for function
 coverage

Add Thread.OnFunctionEnter and Thread.OnFunctionExit callbacks to enable
function-level coverage collection and profiling.

OnFunctionEnter is called when entering a Starlark function (after argument
binding, before execution). OnFunctionExit is called when exiting (via return
or completion), receiving the return value.

Changes:
- Thread.OnFunctionEnter and OnFunctionExit fields in eval.go
- Hook invocations in interp.go CallInternal
- Tests for function call tracking and result capture

Note: The <toplevel> pseudo-function also triggers these hooks during
module execution.

TODO(upstream): trim verbose comments to match codebase style before proposing.
